  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"565\" data-end=\"640\">\n<p data-start=\"567\" data-end=\"640\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"567\" data-end=\"581\">Mesothelin</strong> is a membrane glycoprotein expressed in mesothelial cells.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"641\" data-end=\"811\">\n<p data-start=\"643\" data-end=\"675\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">It is commonly overexpressed in:</span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"678\" data-end=\"811\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"678\" data-end=\"706\">\n<p data-start=\"680\" data-end=\"706\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"680\" data-end=\"706\">Malignant Mesothelioma</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"709\" data-end=\"740\">\n<p data-start=\"711\" data-end=\"740\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"711\" data-end=\"740\">Pancreatic Adenocarcinoma</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"743\" data-end=\"773\">\n<p data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"773\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"773\">Ovarian Serous Carcinoma</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"776\" data-end=\"811\">\n<p data-start=\"778\" data-end=\"811\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"778\" data-end=\"811\">Some Lung and Gastric Cancers</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"812\" data-end=\"927\">\n<p data-start=\"814\" data-end=\"927\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">A <strong data-start=\"816\" data-end=\"835\">positive result</strong> supports the diagnosis of tumors of mesothelial or mesothelin-expressing epithelial origin.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"928\" data-end=\"1058\">\n<p data-start=\"930\" data-end=\"1058\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">It is used as part of an <strong data-start=\"955\" data-end=\"984\">immunohistochemical panel</strong> to distinguish between reactive and malignant mesothelial proliferations.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
